\"]: the attribute [\" + name + \"] is defined multiple times with different types\"\n                );\n            }\n        }\n    }","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"MethodDeclaration","descendantSimpleNames":["validateGrokPattern","grokParser","String","pattern","Map","String","DataType","definedAttributes","HashMap","Attribute","field","grokParser","extractedFields","String","name","field","name","DataType","type","field","dataType","DataType","prev","definedAttributes","put","name","type","prev","ParsingException","pattern","name"],"identifiers":["definedAttributes","field","grokParser","prev","name","pattern","type","validateGrokPattern"],"startLine":157,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":169,"endLineOffset":5,"length":617,"subs":[]}]},{"comment":"The `grokParser` variable was introduced to avoid redundant calls to `Grok.pattern`. However, the code does not handle potential exceptions that might occur during the instantiation of `Grok.Parser`. Unhandled exceptions can lead to system crashes or inconsistent states.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/LogicalPlanBuilder.java-DST-ADDITION-6305-6365-VariableDeclarationStatement","path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/LogicalPlanBuilder.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"Grok.Parser grokParser \u003d Grok.pattern(source(ctx), pattern);","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"VariableDeclarationStatement","descendantSimpleNames":["grokParser","Grok","pattern","source","ctx","pattern"],"identifiers":["grokParser"],"startLine":150,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":150,"endLineOffset":72,"length":61,"subs":[{"startLine":150,"startLineOffset":24,"endLine":150,"endLineOffset":71,"length":48},{"startLine":150,"startLineOffset":37,"endLine":150,"endLineOffset":71,"length":35},{"startLine":150,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":150,"endLineOffset":23,"length":12}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/LogicalPlanBuilder.java-DST-ADDITION-6508-6518-SimpleName","path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/LogicalPlanBuilder.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"grokParser","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"SimpleName","descendantSimpleNames":["grokParser"],"startLine":152,"startLineOffset":88,"endLine":152,"endLineOffset":98,"length":11,"subs":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/LogicalPlanBuilder.java-SRC-SRC_MOVE-6381-6415-MethodInvocation","path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/parser/LogicalPlanBuilder.java","srcDst":"SRC","content":"Grok.pattern(source(ctx), pattern)","nodeType":"SRC_MOVE","treeType":"MethodInvocation","descendantSimpleNames":["Grok","pattern","source","ctx","pattern"],"startLine":150,"startLineOffset":88,"endLine":150,"endLineOffset":122,"length":35,"subs":[]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":165,"line":167,"comment_lines":["[][167]"],"review_comment":["[A quick skim over comment] With EVAL we allow overwriting a field, irrespective of its type. Same with GROK(), when overriding input (i.e. already existing) fields. \r\nWouldn\u0027t it make sense to allow this overriding, generally (i.e. even if different types)? Or, otherwise, reject overriding even if of the same type?","Unfortunately the problem is more subtle here: for the calculation we rely on `org.elasticsearch.grok.Grok`, that is an ingest component, so we have limited control on how we parse the patterns and how we collect results.\r\n\r\nToday we supports patterns like `%{WORD:foo} %{WORD:foo}` (attribute defined twice, same type) because GROK just returns a multi-value. Changing this behavior (ie. rejecting this pattern entirely or returning only one value) would be a breaking change. \r\n\r\nWe could try to support some kind of override in case of different types, but I\u0027m not sure it would be coherent with the behavior described above.","This PR cou